  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 159 PM CDT Tue Sep 22 2026\n\nThursday through Tuesday\nAssessment...medium to high (50-70%) confidence on moderating\ntemperatures. Medium (40-60%) confidence of the wet pattern\nreturning\n\nLow level easterly flow will push moisture west from the nor'easter \non the east coast. While the forecast is mainly dry through Friday, \nsome isolated diurnally driven showers cannot be fully ruled out.\n\nStarting Friday night but especially from Sunday on, the global \nmodels are showing tropical moisture getting pulled north from the \nsystems in the eastern Pacific along with some moisture from the \nwestern Gulf.\n\nThe stronger moisture transport is initially across central and \nwestern Iowa so any rain chances for eastern Iowa would be west of a \nline from Dubuque, IA to Keokuk, IA through the weekend. However, by \nearly next week the tropical moisture transport increases \nconsiderably. With the MJO progged to be cycling between phase 1 and \n8, this increases the probability that the area may experience \nanother period of above normal rainfall.\n\nGiven the very wet pattern we are just completing, another period of \nabove normal rainfall may prolong already high water levels on area \nrivers.",
